<title>UK: Cazenove Indian GDR Index rises 1.4 percent.</title>
<headline>Cazenove Indian GDR Index rises 1.4 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cazenove Indian GDR Index rose 0.82 points, 1.37 percent, to 60.77 after the Bombay Stock Exchange 30 share index rose 70.76 points to a provisional 2,815.82.</p>
<p>The premium for GDRs over stocks on the local market was 11.22 percent.</p>
<p>The Cazenove index is a capitalisation weighted basket of Indian global depositary receipts and measures the change from midday on the previous trading day to midday today.</p>
<p>-- David Chance, London newsroom +44 171 542 5887</p>
